                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] I played this game on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers without any issues [/h1]\n\nSo Flappy Arms and this game released at almost the same time.  They are basically the same game, with some key differences for each.  The mechanics in Flappy Arms feel great and responsive.  The visuals in Flappy Arms were terrible.  The mechanics in Kitty Hawk are more interesting, but are not as responsive.  The visuals are much better in this game.\n\nWhat really differentiates Kitty Hawk is that there is more of a challenge.  I think at times, the challenge is unfair.  I believe the levels are randomly generated.  So you will have a different playthroughs each time.  You will have windmills, shots fired at you, steep declines required, etc.  However, there is really not a way to go down fast.  That's the unfair challenge I believe exists.  You can go up fast by flapping your wings hard, but if then you have to go back down, then you are SOL.  There should be a game mechanic to go down fast and/or slow momentum.\n\nYou can turbo fly by pressing trigger.  That will be how you get around some of the windmill and rotating tower challenges.  You can pick up coins and diamonds.  You can turbo past munitions fired at you.  \n\nI think the visuals would be better without neon all around.  But at least there is a consistent theme.  There is a lot of variety on what you will be trying to fly by.  The music could be better or at least more varied.  \n\nI can recommend this game on sale, but just barely.  Needs tighter controls and better music to be worth a normal price of $2.99.  \n\nSale Price Rating ($1.97) 5.5/10",
